<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiomara Castro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1959">1959</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xiomara Castro (born 1959) is a Honduran politician who was president from January 2022 to January 2026, the first woman to hold the office. The wife of former president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-zelaya">Manuel Zelaya</a>, she led the resistance movement after his removal in 2009 and co-founded the left-wing Libre party. Her government repealed the law on charter cities and switched diplomatic recognition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xiomara-castro.jpg" alt="Xiomara Castro" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fotografía oficial de la Presidencia de Colombia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xiomara_Castro_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
